==Spanish==
{{wp|lang=es}}

===Pronunciation===
{{es-pr|+<audio:LL-Q1321 (spa)-AdrianAbdulBaha-nada.wav<a:Colombia>>}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|es|osp|nada}}, inherited from {{inh|es|la|([[nullus|nūlla]] [[rēs]]) [[natus|nāta]]|lit=no born thing, not a thing born}}, an extension of {{m|la|[[nēmō]] [[nātus]]||not a soul|lit=nobody born}}. For descendants of the other part of the expression see {{ncog|gl|ren||nothing}}, {{ncog|fr|rien||nothing}}, {{ncog|ca|res||nothing; anything}}. For the [[grammaticalization]] of an original nominal as a negative see [[w:Jespersen%27s_Cycle|Jespersen's Cycle]] and {{ncog|fr|personne}}, {{m|fr|pas}}; see also {{m|es|nadie}}, from the same root.

====Pronoun====
{{head|es|pronoun}}

# [[nothing]], [[zero]], [[zilch]], not...[[anything]]
#: {{syn|es|[[ninguna]] [[cosa]]}}
#: {{ux|es|No hay '''nada''' en la mesa.|There is '''nothing''' on the table.}}
#: {{ux|es|'''Nada''' ocurrió ayer.|'''Nothing''' happened yesterday.}}
#: {{ux|es|No veo '''nada'''.|I do'''n’t''' see '''anything'''.}}
#: {{ux|es|Me niego a creer '''nada''' de lo que dice.|I refuse to believe '''anything''' he says.}}
#: {{ux|es|'''Nada''' es eterno.|'''Nothing''' is eternal.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The pronoun requires the verb to be negated if used after the verb; conversely, the verb can't be negated if {{m|es||nada}} precedes it: {{m|es||'''nada''' veo ~ no veo '''nada'''|I don't see anything}}, but *{{m|es||nada no veo ~ veo nada}} are ungrammatical in standard Spanish.

